        "Claude Full review (V-100): changes_requested cycle 1 - 1. CI is red on head e2389d80 (run 37275317330, quality job failed; the two PostgreSQL tests were expected to need CI). Fix and cite a green full run. I cannot read the job log from my environment, so include the failing test names in your response. 2. A normal server-side stop-out or take-profit must not pause trading. reconcile() currently marks a submitted record closed and sets mismatch=True, so every ordinary exit latches a durable pause and needs a manual resume. Treat a submitted record whose deal is gone as closed without mismatch (optionally confirm with get_activity). Also accept a broker position size smaller than the reserved size (partial closes are a supported feature) while still flagging a larger size. Tests: stop-out then submit next cycle works; partial close does not pause; larger size or unknown position still pauses. 3. The Guardian lease is only checked inside submit(), and the lease TTL is 30 s, so after about 30 s idle the next entry finds an expired Guardian lease and pauses the system. tick()/reconcile() must renew both leases every interval. A lost lease still pauses and alerts; no silent re-acquire mid-run. Test with a fake clock or a lease double that expires after idle. 4. There is no deterministic way out of a reserved or ambiguous record, so the first ambiguous order or crash after reservation deadlocks resume() forever (reconcile keeps returning mismatch). Add an operator-only resolve_intent(cycle_id, outcome, deal_id=None, reason) that works only while paused, never resends, is journaled with an alert, and is not reachable from any LLM-side module. Outcomes: matched (link to a broker position whose epic/direction/size/stop match the intent) or rejected (only when broker positions and get_activity show nothing for that dealReference). Use the get_activity result rather than discarding it. Tests: timeout-after-accept then resolve matched then resume works with no resubmission; process killed after reserve then resolve rejected then resume works and the cycle_id is still never reusable. 5. Acceptance criterion 'test that the LLM-side modules cannot reach it' is not covered: the AST test only proves place_order has one caller. Add an import-boundary test that nothing under agents/, lab/ or other LLM-side packages imports trader.execution.manager, journal, leader, reconciliation or brokers, directly or transitively.",
